// A freestanding program that measures what the runtime's free lists give back:
// the arena's high-water mark after a thousand lists the compiler frees, and
// after a thousand it cannot (each one is returned, so it is kept). It stands
// in for a kernel only as far as boot.S needs: id_main to run, and the id_kpanic
// that isr.S names.
main(int argc, string[] argv) {
  word fr = growth(0);
  word kp = growth(1);
  print("kfree freed=" + fr + " kept=" + kp);
} return int 0;

kpanic(word vec, word e, word p) {
} return void;
